# Sources:
#   https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qtqml-documents-definetypes.html
# Verified on Qt 6.11.2 (qml6, offscreen).

@qt-parity
Feature: The buttons of the components example
  A file Button.qml makes a type Button, which application.qml uses three
  times in a column: red, blue and moved right, red again.

  Background:
    Given the file "Button.qml":
      """qml
{{Button.qml}}
      """
    And the file "application.qml":
      """qml
{{application.qml}}
      """

  Scenario: The three buttons stand in a column
    When "application.qml" is loaded
    Then the pixel at 25, 25 of the window is "#ff0000"
    And the pixel at 100, 75 of the window is "#0000ff"
    And the pixel at 25, 125 of the window is "#ff0000"

  Scenario: The second button is moved right of the column's edge
    When "application.qml" is loaded
    Then the pixel at 55, 75 of the window is "#0000ff"
    And the pixel at 140, 75 of the window is "#0000ff"

  Scenario: A click on a button leaves the column as it was
    When "application.qml" is loaded
    And the user presses the pointer at 100, 75
    And the user releases the pointer at 100, 75
    Then the pixel at 100, 75 of the window is "#0000ff"
    And the pixel at 25, 25 of the window is "#ff0000"
